hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6877","The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) hurried towards it, until only twelve people remained with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you had all gone after them so that none of you remained, this entire valley would have been filled with fire for you."" (The narrator says:) Regarding this, the following verse was revealed: ""And when they saw a transaction or a diversion, they rushed to it and left you standing (delivering the sermon)."" The narrator said: Among those twelve people who remained with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) were Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6878","While I was asleep I saw (in a dream) a cup containing milk being presented to me. I took out of that until I perceived freshness being reflected through my nails. Then I presented the leftover to 'Umar b. Khattab. They said: Messenger of Allah: How do you interpret it? He said: This implies knowledge. (Using translation from Muslim 2391a)"
"6879","I was with him. I was walking behind him, and whatever I saw, I understood and heard. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to that person and said: O Jameel, I have accepted Islam. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: By Allah! He did not reply to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) until he went with him towards Masjid al-Haram, and among the gatherings of Quraysh, he announced: O group of Quraysh! The son of Khattab has become irreligious. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He has lied; rather, I have accepted Islam, and I have believed in Allah Almighty, and I have affirmed His Messenger. Then those people attacked Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) also started fighting with them, until the sun set over their heads (i.e., the fight continued for quite a while), until Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sat down separately. Those people were standing at the head of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Do whatever you think is appropriate. By Allah! If we become three hundred people, then either you will leave it for us, or we will leave it for you. While those people were still standing by Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), a man came who was wearing a silk cloak and a Qumasi shirt. He inquired: What is the matter with you people? They replied: The son of Khattab has become irreligious. He said: Leave him, for a man has chosen a religion for himself. Do you think that Banu Adi will hand over their companion (i.e., one of their men) to you? The narrator says: It was as if a veil had been over their eyes, which was now lifted. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: Later, in Madinah Munawwarah, I asked Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): Father, who was that person who turned the others away from you that day? Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: O my son, that was As bin Wa'il."
"6880","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Since Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted Islam, we have continuously remained dominant."
"6881","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) made a supplication: ""O Allah, honor Islam through the one who is more beloved to You of these two men—Abu Jahl bin Hisham or Umar bin Khattab."" (The narrator says:) So, the one who was more beloved to Allah among the two was Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6882","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'O Allah! Strengthen Islam with 'Umar bin Khattab in particular.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 105)"
"6883","narrates: When Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted Islam, Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), the inhabitants of the heavens (angels) are rejoicing at Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) accepting Islam."
"6884","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Umar bin Khattab is among the people of Paradise."
"6885","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Aisha."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Among the men, who is it?"" He said, ""Her father, Abu Bakr."" I asked, ""Then who?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then Umar bin Khattab."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned some other people."
"6886","The people replied: This is the palace of Umar bin Khattab. So I did not enter it only because I know of your (Umar's) temperament and sharpness. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, would I ever show sharpness of temperament against you, would I ever show sharpness of temperament against you?"
"6887","that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""I entered Paradise and it was as if I was in a palace of gold. So I said: 'Whose palace is this?' They said: 'A youth's, from the Quraish.' So I thought that I was him. I said: 'And who is he?' They said: ""'Umar bin Al-Khattab."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3688)"
"6888","""We were sitting with the Prophet and he said: 'While I was sleeping I saw myself in Paradise (in a dream), and I saw a woman performing ablution beside a palace. I asked: ""Whose palace is this?"" She said: ""'Umar's."" I remembered his protective jealousy, so I turned away and left.'"" Abu Hurairah said: ''Umar wept and said: 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! Would I feel any protective jealousy against you?'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 107)"
"6889","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah, the Exalted, has placed truth on Umar's tongue and he speaks it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2962)"
"6890","""While I was sleeping I saw people presented before me, and that they were wearing shirts. Some of them (the shirts) reaching their breasts, and some of them reaching below that."" He said: ""Then 'Umar was presented before me and he was wearing a shirt that was dragging."" They said: ""How did you interpret that O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""The religion."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2285)"
"6891","I would give it as ransom."
"6892","I know that Satan flees from you."
"6893","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O enemies of your own souls! You fear me but do not fear the Messenger of Allah? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Umar! If Satan were to encounter you on a path, he would leave that path and take another."
"6894","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Among the nations, there used to be Muhaddathun (those who were given understanding), and if there were one in my nation, it would be 'Umar bin Al-Khattab."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3693)"
"6895","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, Allah the Exalted has placed the truth upon Umar's tongue and heart (or made it flow from them)."" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: Whenever a situation arose in which people held one opinion and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) held another opinion, the Qur'an was revealed in accordance with Sayyiduna Umar's (may Allah be pleased with him) opinion."
"6896","I agreed with my Lord, may He be glorified and exalted, in three matters - or my Lord agreed with me in three matters, I said: O Messenger of Allah, why don't you take the Maqarn of Ibraheem as a place of prayer? Then Allah revealed the verse: ʿAnd take you (people) the Maqam (place) of Ibraheem (Abraham) [or the stone on which Ibraheem (Abraham) stood while he was building the Ka'bah) as a place of prayerʿ (al Baqarah 2:125). And I said: Why don't you tell the Mothers of the Believers to observe hijab, for both righteous people and evildoers enter upon you? Then the verse of hijab was revealed. And I heard something about the Mothers of the Believers, so I talked to them and told them: You should stop bothering the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , or Allah will replace you with wives who are better than you and are Muslims. Then I came to one of the Mothers of the Believers and she said: O 'Umar, is it the case that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cannot admonish his wives so that you come and admonish them? So I stopped, then Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, revealed the verse: “It may be if he divorced you (all) that his Lord will give him instead of you, wives better than you Muslims (who submit to Allah), believers, obedient (to Allah)...ʿ [at­-Tahreerm 66:5) (Using translation from Aḥmad 160)"
"6897","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a white garment on Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked: ""Is your shirt new or washed?"" He replied: ""It is new."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wear new clothes, live a praiseworthy life, and die as a martyr."" Imam Abdur Razzaq says: The narrator named Thawri has additionally narrated from Ismail bin Abu Khalid these words: ""May Allah grant you the coolness of the eyes in this world and the Hereafter."
"6898","While I was asleep I saw myself on a well with a leathern bucket on a pulley. I drew (water) out of that as Allah wished me (to draw). Then the son of Abu Quhafa (Abu Bakr) drew from it one bucketful or two and there was some weakness in drawing that (may Allah forgive him). Then that bucket (changed into a large bucket) and Ibn Khattab drew it. I did not see any strongest man drawing it like 'Umar b. Khattab. He brought out so much water that the camels of the people had enough to drink and then laid down (for rest). (Using translation from Muslim 2392a)"
"6899","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I am the first for whom the earth will split, then Abu Bakr, then 'Umar. Then the people of Al-Baqi; they will be gathered with me. Then I will await the people of Makkah until they are resurrected between the Two Sacred areas."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3692)"
"6900","The Prophet ﷺ deputed me to read the Army of Dhat-as-Salasil. I came to him and said, ""Who is the most beloved person to you?"" He said, "" ʿAisha."" I asked, ""Among the men?"" He said, ""Her father."" I said, ""Who then?"" He said, ""Then ʿUmar bin Al-Khattab."" He then named other men. (Using translation from Bukhārī 3662)"
"6901","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If people obey Abu Bakr and Umar, they will be rightly guided."
"6902","The Prophet (peace be upon him) pointed towards Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: And act upon the guidance of Ammar, and accept whatever Abdullah bin Mas'ud tells you."
"6903","The cow turned towards him and said: 'We have not been created for this purpose; we have been created for plowing.' The people said: 'Subhan Allah, Subhan Allah.' The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'I, Abu Bakr, and Umar also believe in this (that the cow can speak), even though these two gentlemen were not present among those people.' The narrator says: So the people said: 'We also believe in that which the Messenger of Allah believes in.'"
"6904","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Abu Bakr and 'Umar are the leaders of the mature people of Paradise, the first and the last, except for the Prophets and the Messengers.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 100)"
"6905","I have been killed. Then the people began to praise him and say: O Leader of the Believers, may Allah reward you with good. You were such and such, and such and such. Then those people left and others came and continued to praise him. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah! Despite what you are saying, I wish that I could be freed from this (government) matter on equal terms, with nothing due from me and nothing for me. Indeed, being a companion of the Messenger of Allah is sufficient for my safety. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who was present at his bedside, began to speak. He was so close to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) as if he were a member of his family. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to recite the Qur’an to him. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: No, by Allah! You will not leave this matter on equal terms. You kept the company of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), you were with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was as pleased with you as he could be with the best of those who were with him. Your status in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was this, this, and this, until when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, he was pleased with you. After that, you were with the Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, you implemented his rule, you did this for him and that for him. O Leader of the Believers! After that, you became the ruler, and you became as good a ruler as anyone could be. You did this and that. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) felt comfort from the words of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: Repeat your words to me. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) repeated them before him. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah! Despite what you are saying, (I believe) that if all the earth were turned to gold for me, I would give it as ransom today against the terror of death. I have established a council of six men: Uthman, Ali bin Abi Talib, Talhah bin Ubaidullah, Zubair bin al-Awwam, Abdur Rahman bin Awf, and Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with them). Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) appointed Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) as an advisor to them, but did not make him a member. He gave them three days’ respite (to select a caliph from among themselves within three days). Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) instructed Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) to lead the people in prayer. May Allah’s mercy and His pleasure descend upon Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6906","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted him permission. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fulfilled his need and remained in the same state under the sheet, then he (Abu Bakr) departed. Then Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted him permission. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fulfilled his need, but he (peace and blessings be upon him) remained in the same state under the sheet, then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) departed. Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) adjusted his clothes and sat up straight, then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fulfilled his need, then he (Uthman) departed. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission to enter upon you, you fulfilled his need but remained in the same state, then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission to enter upon you, you fulfilled his need but remained in the same state, then Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission to enter upon you, so you adjusted your clothes and sat up straight."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aisha! Uthman is a modest man, if I had permitted him in that state, I feared that he would not have expressed his need before me."
"6907","Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lying in the bed in my apartment with his thigh uncovered and Abu Bakr sought permission to enter. It was given to him and he conversed in the same very state (the Prophet's thigh or shank uncovered). Then ʿUmar sought permission for entering and it was given to him and he conversed in that very state. Then ʿUthman sought permission to enter; Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and he set right his clothes. Muhammad (one of the narrators) said: I do not say that it happened on the same day. He (ʿUthman) then entered and conversed and as he went out, ʿAisha said: Abu Bakr entered and you did not stir and did not observe much care (in arranging your clothes), then ʿUmar entered and you did not stir and did not arrange your clothes, then ʿUthman entered and you got up and set your clothes right, so he ﷺ said: Should I not show modesty to one whom even the Angels show modesty. (Using translation from Muslim 2401)"
"6908","The prophet of Allah ﷺ ascended Uhud, and Abu Bakr, ’Umar and 'Uthman followed him. It began to shake with them. The prophet of Allah ﷺ struck it with his foot and said: Be still, for only a prophet, an ever-truthful and two martyrs are on you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4651)"
"6909","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had sent Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) on some of his work at the time of the Battle of Badr, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fixed a share for Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) (in the spoils of Badr). The man said: I asked you whether he was present at the Pledge of Ridwan, and you replied: No. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had sent him on his personal work, then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed one of his hands on the other (and pledged allegiance on behalf of Sayyiduna Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him). So tell me, which hand was better: the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) or the hand of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)? The man said: I asked you whether he was among those who turned back on the day when the two groups faced each other, and you replied: Yes. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Allah the Exalted has said: “They slipped because of some of what they had done, but Allah has pardoned them. Surely Allah is Forgiving, Forbearing.” (Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said to that man) Now go and do your utmost."
"6910","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Open the door for him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise. He was Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him). Then another man came and asked for the door to be opened. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Open the door for him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise. He was Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). Then another man came and asked for the door to be opened. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Open the door for him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise. He was Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6911","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me, ""Watch the door."" Then a man came and sought permission to enter. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Give him permission and give him the glad tidings of Paradise."" He was Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him). Then another man came and sought permission to enter. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Give him permission and give him the glad tidings of Paradise."" He was Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Then another man came and sought permission to enter. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent, then he said, ""Give him permission, give him the glad tidings of Paradise, and along with it, he will face a severe trial that will befall him."" He was Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6912","Open it for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise and, lo, it was Abu Bakr. I opened (the gate) for him and gave him the glad tidings of Paradise. Then another person asked for the door to be opened, whereupon he said: Open it and give him the glad tidings of Piradise. He said: I went away and, lo, it was 'Umar. I opened it for him and gave him the glad tidings of Paradise. Then still another man asked for the door to be opened, and thereupon Allah's Apostle ﷺ said: Open it and give him the glad tidings of Paradise after a trial would afflict him. I went and, lo, it was 'Uthman b. 'Affan. 1 opened the door and gave him the glad tidings of Paradise and informed him (what the Prophet had said). Thereupon he said: O Allah, grant me steadfastness. Allah is one Whose help is to be sought. (Using translation from Muslim 2403a)"
"6913","Last night a good man had a vision in which Abu Bakr seemed to be joined to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ‘Umar to Abu Bakr, and ‘Uthman to ‘Umar. Jabir said: When we got up and left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we said: The good man is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that their being joined together means that they are the rulers over this matter with which Allah has sent His Prophet ﷺ. Abu Dawud said: It has been transmitted by Yunus and Shu’aib, but they did not mention ‘Amr b. Aban. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4636)"
"6914","I quickly rushed towards the person to whom the Prophet (peace be upon him) had indicated and asked: O Messenger of Allah, is it this one? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Yes, it is he. And that was Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6915","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I wish there was someone with whom we could converse. I said: O Messenger of Allah! I will send a message to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him); he will come and converse with us. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. Sayyidah Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! I will send a message to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him); he will come and converse with us. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called a man and spoke to him in a whisper, the content of which did not reach us, then the man left. Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) came, then that man left, then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned towards him. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “O Uthman! Indeed, Allah will clothe you with a shirt, and people will wish that you take it off, but do not take it off.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this three times. Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I said: O Mother of the Believers, why did you not narrate this hadith earlier? So Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O my son, I had forgotten it as if I had never heard it. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abdullah bin Qais Lakhmi passed away in 124 Hijri. He is not the same Abdullah bin Abu Qais who was a student of Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"6916","""When 'Uthman was besieged, he looked out over them from atop his house and said: 'I remind you by Allah. Do you know that when (mount) Hira shook, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Be firm O Hira! For there is none upon you except a Prophet, a Siddiq, and a martyr?""' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I remind you by Allah! Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, about the army of distress (Al-'Usrah): ""Who will spend something which shall be accepted (by Allah)?"" And the people were struggling during difficult times, so I prepared that army?' They said: 'Yes.' Then he said: 'I remind you by Allah. Do you know that no one drank from the well of Rumah but have to pay for it, then I bought it and made it for the rich, the poor, and the wayfarer?' They said: 'O Allah! Yes!'"" And he listed other things. This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib from this route; as a narration of Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami from 'Uthman. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3699)"
"6917","I saw ʿUmar bin Al-Khattab a few days before he was stabbed in Medina. He was standing with Hudhaifa bin Al-Yaman and ʿUthman bin Hunaif to whom he said, ""What have you done? Do you think that you have imposed more taxation on the land (of As-Swad i.e. 'Iraq) than it can bear?"" They replied, ""We have imposed on it what it can bear because of its great yield."" ʿUmar again said, ""Check whether you have imposed on the land what it can not bear."" They said, ""No, (we haven't)."" ʿUmar added, ""If Allah should keep me alive I will let the widows of Iraq need no men to support them after me."" But only four days had elapsed when he was stabbed (to death ). The day he was stabbed, I was standing and there was nobody between me and him (i.e. ʿUmar) except ʿAbdullah bin ʿAbbas. Whenever ʿUmar passed between the two rows, he would say, ""Stand in straight lines."" When he saw no defect (in the rows), he would go forward and start the prayer with Takbir. He would recite Surat Yusuf or An-Nahl or the like in the first rakʿa so that the people may have the time to Join the prayer. As soon as he said Takbir, I heard him saying, ""The dog has killed or eaten me,"" at the time he (i.e. the murderer) stabbed him. A non-Arab infidel proceeded on carrying a double-edged knife and stabbing all the persons he passed by on the right and left (till) he stabbed thirteen persons out of whom seven died. When one of the Muslims saw that, he threw a cloak on him. Realizing that he had been captured, the non-Arab infidel killed himself, ʿUmar held the hand of ʿAbdur-Rahman bin ʿAuf and let him lead the prayer. Those who were standing by the side of ʿUmar saw what I saw, but the people who were in the other parts of the Mosque did not see anything, but they lost the voice of ʿUmar and they were saying, ""Subhan Allah! Subhan Allah! (i.e. Glorified be Allah)."" ʿAbdur-Rahman bin ʿAuf led the people a short prayer. When they finished the prayer, ʿUmar said, ""O Ibn ʿAbbas! Find out who attacked me."" Ibn ʿAbbas kept on looking here and there for a short time and came to say. ""The slave of Al Mughira."" On that ʿUmar said, ""The craftsman?"" Ibn ʿAbbas said, ""Yes."" ʿUmar said, ""May Allah curse him. I did not treat him unjustly. All the Praises are for Allah Who has not caused me to die at the hand of a man who claims himself to be a Muslim. No doubt, you and your father (Abbas) used to love to have more non-Arab infidels in Medina."" Al-Abbas had the greatest number of slaves. Ibn ʿAbbas said to ʿUmar. ""If you wish, we will do."" He meant, ""If you wish we will kill them."" ʿUmar said, ""You are mistaken (for you can't kill them) after they have spoken your language, prayed towards your Qibla, and performed Hajj like yours."" Then ʿUmar was carried to his house, and we went along with him, and the people were as if they had never suffered a calamity before. Some said, ""Do not worry (he will be Alright soon)."" Some said, ""We are afraid (that he will die)."" Then an infusion of dates was brought to him and he drank it but it came out (of the wound) of his belly. Then milk was brought to him and he drank it, and it also came out of his belly. The people realized that he would die. We went to him, and the people came, praising him. A young man came saying, ""O chief of the believers! Receive the glad tidings from Allah to you due to your company with Messenger of Allah ﷺ and your superiority in Islam which you know. Then you became the ruler (i.e. Caliph) and you ruled with justice and finally you have been martyred."" ʿUmar said, ""I wish that all these privileges will counterbalance (my shortcomings) so that I will neither lose nor gain anything."" When the young man turned back to leave, his clothes seemed to be touching the ground. ʿUmar said, ""Call the young man back to me."" (When he came back) ʿUmar said, ""O son of my brother! Lift your clothes, for this will keep your clothes clean and save you from the Punishment of your Lord."" ʿUmar further said, ""O ʿAbdullah bin ʿUmar! See how much I am in debt to others."" When the debt was checked, it amounted to approximately eighty-six thousand. ʿUmar said, ""If the property of ʿUmar's family covers the debt, then pay the debt thereof; otherwise request it from Bani ʿAdi bin Kaʿb, and if that too is not sufficient, ask for it from Quraish tribe, and do not ask for it from any one else, and pay this debt on my behalf."" ʿUmar then said (to ʿAbdullah), ""Go to ʿAisha (the mother of the believers) and say: ""ʿUmar is paying his salutation to you. But don't say: 'The chief of the believers,' because today I am not the chief of the believers. And say: ""ʿUmar bin Al-Khattab asks the permission to be buried with his two companions (i.e. the Prophet, and Abu Bakr)."" ʿAbdullah greeted ʿAisha and asked for the permission for entering, and then entered to her and found her sitting and weeping. He said to her, ""ʿUmar bin Al-Khattab is paying his salutations to you, and asks the permission to be buried with his two companions."" She said, ""I had the idea of having this place for myself, but today I prefer ʿUmar to myself."" When he returned it was said (to ʿUmar), ""ʿAbdullah bin ʿUmar has come."" ʿUmar said, ""Make me sit up."" Somebody supported him against his body and ʿUmar asked (ʿAbdullah), ""What news do you have?"" He said, ""O chief of the believers! It is as you wish. She has given the permission."" ʿUmar said, ""Praise be to Allah, there was nothing more important to me than this. So when I die, take me, and greet ʿAisha and say: ""ʿUmar bin Al-Khattab asks the permission (to be buried with the Prophet ﷺ ), and if she gives the permission, bury me there, and if she refuses, then take me to the grave-yard of the Muslims."" Then Hafsa (the mother of the believers) came with many other women walking with her. When we saw her, we went away. She went in (to ʿUmar) and wept there for sometime. When the men asked for permission to enter, she went into another place, and we heard her weeping inside. The people said (to ʿUmar), ""O chief of the believers! Appoint a successor."" ʿUmar said, ""I do not find anyone more suitable for the job than the following persons or group whom Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been pleased with before he died."" Then ʿUmar mentioned ʿAli, ʿUthman, AzZubair, Talha, Saʿd and ʿAbdur-Rahman (bin ʿAuf) and said, ""Abdullah bin ʿUmar will be a witness to you, but he will have no share in the rule. His being a witness will compensate him for not sharing the right of ruling. If Saʿd becomes the ruler, it will be alright: otherwise, whoever becomes the ruler should seek his help, as I have not dismissed him because of disability or dishonesty."" ʿUmar added, ""I recommend that my successor takes care of the early emigrants; to know their rights and protect their honor and sacred things. I also recommend that he be kind to the Ansar who had lived in Medina before the emigrants and Belief had entered their hearts before them. I recommend that the (ruler) should accept the good of the righteous among them and excuse their wrong-doers, and I recommend that he should do good to all the people of the towns (Al-Ansar), as they are the protectors of Islam and the source of wealth and the source of annoyance to the enemy. I also recommend that nothing be taken from them except from their surplus with their consent. I also recommend that he do good to the 'Arab bedouin, as they are the origin of the 'Arabs and the material of Islam. He should take from what is inferior, amongst their properties and distribute that to the poor amongst them. I also recommend him concerning Allah's and His Apostle's protectees (i.e. Dhimmis) to fulfill their contracts and to fight for them and not to overburden them with what is beyond their ability."" So when ʿUmar expired, we carried him out and set out walking. ʿAbdullah bin ʿUmar greeted (ʿAisha) and said, ""ʿUmar bin Al-Khattab asks for the permission."" ʿAisha said, ""Bring him in."" He was brought in and buried beside his two companions. When he was buried, the group (recommended by ʿUmar) held a meeting. Then ʿAbdur-Rahman said, "" Reduce the candidates for rulership to three of you."" Az-Zubair said, ""I give up my right to ʿAli."" Talha said, ""I give up my right to ʿUthman,"" Saʿd, 'I give up my right to ʿAbdur-Rahman bin ʿAuf."" ʿAbdur-Rahman then said (to ʿUthman and ʿAli), ""Now which of you is willing to give up his right of candidacy to that he may choose the better of the (remaining) two, bearing in mind that Allah and Islam will be his witnesses."" So both the sheiks (i.e. ʿUthman and ʿAli) kept silent. ʿAbdur-Rahman said, ""Will you both leave this matter to me, and I take Allah as my Witness that I will not choose but the better of you?"" They said, ""Yes."" So ʿAbdur-Rahman took the hand of one of them (i.e. ʿAli) and said, ""You are related to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and one of the earliest Muslims as you know well. So I ask you by Allah to promise that if I select you as a ruler you will do justice, and if I select ʿUthman as a ruler you will listen to him and obey him."" Then he took the other (i.e. ʿUthman) aside and said the same to him. When ʿAbdur-Rahman secured (their agreement to) this covenant, he said, ""O ʿUthman! Raise your hand."" So he (i.e. ʿAbdur-Rahman) gave him (i.e. ʿUthman) the solemn pledge, and then ʿAli gave him the pledge of allegiance and then all the (Medina) people gave him the pledge of allegiance. (Using translation from Bukhārī 3700)"
"6918","""When he was ill, the Messenger of Allah said: 'I would like to have some of my Companions with me.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Shall we call Abu Bakr for you?' But he remained silent. We said: 'Shall we call 'Umar for you?' But he remained silent. We said: 'Shall we call 'Uthman for you?' He said: 'Yes.' So 'Uthman came and he spoke to him in private. The Prophet started to speak to him and 'Uthman's expression changed."" Qais said: ""Abu Sahlah, the freed slave of 'Uthman, narrated to me that on the Day of the House, 'Uthman bin 'Affan said: 'The Messenger of Allah told me what would come to pass and now I am coming to that day.'""In his narration of the Hadith, 'Ali (one of the narrators) said (that he said): ""And I am going to bear it with patience."" Qais said: ""They used to think that that was the Day of the House."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 113)"
"6920","""We set out as pilgrims and came to Al-Madinah intending to perform Hajj. While we were in our camping place unloading our mounts, someone came to us and said: 'The people have gathered in the Masjid and there is panis.' So we set out and found the people gathered around a group in the middle of the Masjid, among whom were 'Ali, Zubayr, Talhah and Sa'd bin Abi Waqas. While we were like that, 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, came, wearing a yellow cloak with which he had covered his head. He said: 'Is Talhah here? Is Az-Zubair here? Is Sa'd here?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I adjure you be the One beside Whom there is none worthy of worship, din't the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever buys the Mirbad [1] of Banu so-and so, Allah will forgive him, and I bought it for twenty or twenty-five thousand, then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him, and he said: Add it to our Masjid and the reward for it will be yours?' They said: 'By Allah, yes.' He said: 'I adjure you by the One beside Whom there is none worthy of worship, didn't the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever buys the well of Rumah, Allah will forgive him, so I bought it for such and such and amount, then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him, and he said: Give it to provide water for the Muslims, and the reward for it will be yours?' They said: 'By Allah, yes.' He said: 'I adjure you by the One beside Whom there is none worthy of worship, didn't the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever equips these (men)- meaning the army of Al-'Usrah (Tabuk) - Allah will forgive him, so I equipped them until they were not lacking even a rope or a bridle?' They said: 'By Allah, yes.' He said: 'O Allah, bear witness, O Allah, bear witness, O Allah, bear witness.'"" [1] Mirbad: A place for drying dates. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3182)"
"6921","Fatima complained of the suffering caused to her by the hand mill. Some Captives were brought to the Prophet, she came to him but did not find him at home ʿAisha was present there to whom she told (of her desire for a servant). When the Prophet ﷺ came, Aisha informed him about Fatima's visit. ʿAli added ""So the Prophet ﷺ came to us, while we had gone to our bed I wanted to get up but the Prophet ﷺ said, ""Remain at your place"". Then he sat down between us till I found the coolness of his feet on my chest. Then he said, ""Shall I teach you a thing which is better than what you have asked me? When you go to bed, say, 'Allahu-Akbar' thirty-four times, and 'Subhan Allah thirty-three times, and 'Al hamdu-li l-lah thirty-three times for that is better for you both than a servant."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3705)"
"6922","Fatimah complained to me about the flour, so I said, ""Why don't you go to your father and ask him for a servant?"" She went to the Prophet ﷺ to request a servant but did not find him. She returned to her place. When the Prophet ﷺ came, he was wearing a garment with a fringe at the bottom, and when we wore it lengthwise, our feet would extend beyond it, and when we wore it widthwise, our heads and feet would protrude."",""The Prophet ﷺ asked Fatimah"",""""""Did you come earlier with a need?"""" She replied"","" """"No."""" I said"","" """"Yes"","" she complained to me about the flour"","" and I suggested she ask her father for a servant."""" The Prophet ﷺ said"","" """"Shall I guide you to something better for the two of you than having a servant? When you go to bed"","" say 'SubhanAllah' (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times"","" 'Alhamdulillah' (Praise be to Allah) thirty-three times"","" and 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) thirty-four times."""""""""
"6923","I do not like that I should cause you any harm."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Whoever causes harm to Ali has caused harm to me."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narrator is Fadl bin Abdullah bin Muqil bin Sinan Ashja'i. Ibn Ishaq has attributed him to his grandfather, while the narrator named Mas'ud bin Sa'd, who is a Kufan, his kunyah is Abu Sa'd."
"6924","'Ali observed: By Him Who split up the seed and created something living, the Apostle (may peace and blessings be upon him) gave me a promise that no one but a believer would love me, and none but a hypocrite would nurse grudge against me. (Using translation from Muslim 78)"
"6925","I say? He said: You should call him Abu Turab. So Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) laughed and said: By Allah! This name was given to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) by the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this name was the most beloved to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). Once, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), then he left (the house), then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: Where is your cousin? She replied: He is sleeping in the mosque. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went there and found him in such a state that his cloak had slipped from his side (and there was dust on his body). So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to wipe the dust from his back and said: O Abu Turab, get up. (Sayyiduna Sahl [may Allah be pleased with him] said:) By Allah! There was no name more beloved to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) than this; the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given him this name."
"6926","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): “Your relation to me is like tha"
"6927","Messenger of Allah, are you leaving me behind amongst women and children? Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: Aren't you satisfied with being unto me what Aaron was unto Moses but with this exception that there would be no prophet after me? (Using translation from Muslim 2404b)"
"6928","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Shall I not teach you some words that if you say them, you will be forgiven, even though you are already forgiven. There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous; there is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Almighty, Glory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the mighty Throne, praise be to Allah the Lord of the Worlds.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 712)"
"6929","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an army and he put 'Ali bin Abi Talib in charge of it. He left on the expedition and he entered upon a female slave. So four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ scolded him, and they made a pact saying: ""[If] we meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we will inform him of what 'Ali did."" When the Muslims returned from the journey, they would begin with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and give him Salam, then they would go to their homes. So when the expedition arrived, they gave Salam to the Prophet ﷺ, and one of the four stood saying: ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you see that 'Ali bin Abi Talib did such and such."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. Then the second one stood and said as he said, and he turned away from him. Then the third stood before him, and said as he said, and he turned away from him. Then the fourth stood and said as they had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced him, and the anger was visible on his face, he said: ""What do you want from 'Ali?! What do you want from 'Ali?! What do you want from 'Ali?! Indeed 'Ali is from me, and I am from him, and he is the ally of every believer after me."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3712)"
"6930","I am the guardian of, Ali is also his guardian."
"6931","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do you not know that I am dearer to the believers than their own selves? They replied: Yes, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: So whomever I am beloved to, this (i.e., Ali) is also beloved to him. O Allah, love the one who loves him and be hostile to the one who is hostile to him. The narrator says: I returned from there, and there was some confusion in my mind regarding this. I met Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned this matter to him. He informed me: I also heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say this about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). The narrator named Abu Nu'aym says: I asked the narrator named Fitr: There is such a gap between those people and their death, so he replied: One hundred days. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) What is meant is the death of Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6932","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Tomorrow I will give the flag to a man with whose leadership Allah will grant (the Muslim) victory."" So the people kept on thinking the whole night as to who would be given the flag. The next morning the people went to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and every one of them hoped that he would be given the flag. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Where is ʿAli bin Abi Talib?"" The people replied, ""He is suffering from eye trouble, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" He said, ""Send for him and bring him to me."" So when ʿAli came, the Prophet ﷺ spat in his eyes and invoked good on him, and be became alright as if he had no ailment. The Prophet ﷺ then gave him the flag. ʿAli said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Shall I fight them (i.e. enemy) till they become like us?"" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Proceed to them steadily till you approach near to them and then invite them to Islam and inform them of their duties towards Allah which Islam prescribes for them, for by Allah, if one man is guided on the right path (i.e. converted to Islam) through you, it would be better for you than (a great number of) red camels."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3701)"
"6933","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Where is Ali?"" People informed: ""His eyes are sore."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) called him, put his saliva on his palm, and rubbed those palms on the eyes of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him the flag, and Allah Almighty granted victory at his hands."
"6934","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): ""You stand up,"" then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entrusted the flag to him and said: ""Go, and do not turn here and there until Allah grants you victory."" He had gone only a little distance, then stopped; he did not look here and there and asked: ""On what basis should I fight the people?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fight them until they testify that there is no deity except Allah. When they say this statement, they will secure their lives and their wealth, except for the right due from them; their reckoning is with Allah."
"6935","I am Marhab, I brandish weapons and am an experienced warrior, at the time when the battle blazes.” So Sayyiduna ‘Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) entered the field and said: “Khaybar knows that I am ‘Amir, I am an experienced warrior carrying weapons.” The two attacked each other, and Marhab’s sword struck Sayyiduna ‘Amir’s (may Allah be pleased with him) horse, then it became unsteady, and his own sword turned back on him and cut his vein, and because of this he passed away. Some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘Amir’s deed has become void, because he killed himself. I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) weeping and said: O Messenger of Allah! Sayyiduna ‘Amir’s (may Allah be pleased with him) deed has become void. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Who said this? I said: Some of your companions are saying this. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, rather he will have a double reward. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me to Sayyiduna ‘Ali bin Abi Talib. I went to him and his eyes were sore. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Today I will give the flag to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and Allah and His Messenger love him. I took Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) by the hand and brought him; his eyes were sore. I brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) applied his saliva to his eyes and he was cured. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him the flag. Then Marhab came out again and recited the same poetry: “Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, I brandish weapons and am an experienced warrior, at the time when the battle blazes.” So Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “I am the one whose mother named him Haydar, like a lion of the forest, who is feared when seen. I measure with the large measure (meaning I kill the enemy swiftly and in great numbers).” The narrator says: Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) struck him and split Marhab’s head, killing him, and victory was granted at the hands of Sayyiduna ‘Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Abu Khalifah narrated these words as such, that the blow was struck on Sayyiduna ‘Amir’s (may Allah be pleased with him) horse, whereas in reality, it was struck on Sayyiduna ‘Amir’s (may Allah be pleased with him) shield."
"6936","Sayyiduna Imam Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) standing and delivering a sermon to the people. (This was the day after the martyrdom of Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him.) He said: ""O people! Yesterday, a person departed from you whom none could surpass, and those who come after cannot reach him. Allah's Messenger sent him on an expedition and gave him the flag, and he did not return until Allah granted him victory. Jibreel was on his right side and Mikaeel was on his left side. He did not leave behind anything of white or yellow (i.e., gold or silver), except for seven hundred dirhams which remained from his salary, and he intended to buy a servant with it."
"6937","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! Will I be that person? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, rather it will be the one who is mending the shoe. The narrator states: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had given his shoe to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) so that he could mend it."
"6938","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿThere will emerge some people among whom is a man with a defective arm, or an incomplete arm, or a small arm.ʿ If you could exercise restraint, I would have told you what Allah promised on the lips of Muhammad ﷺ to those who kill them. ‘Abeedah said to ʿAli ؓ Did you hear that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah; yes, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah, yes, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah. (Using translation from Aḥmad 735)"
"6939","I am seeing that appearance among these people. These people speak the truth with their tongues (i.e., they recite the Qur’an), but it does not go beyond this. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) pointed to his throat and said: And they are the most hated of Allah’s creation in the sight of Allah. Among them is a black man whose one hand is like a woman’s breast. When Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) killed those people, he said: Examine this matter. When they examined, they did not find that man. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Go back! By Allah, neither have I lied nor has I been lied to. He said this two or perhaps three times. Then such a man was found by those people in a ruin. They brought him until they placed him before Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). The narrator named Ubaidullah says: I was present at the incident of these (Khawarij) and at the time of Sayyiduna Ali’s (may Allah be pleased with him) statement about them."
"6940","I fell sick and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me when I was saying O Allah, if my time has come then grant me relief; if it has not yet come then raise me in status; and if this is a trial then grant me patience. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What did you say?” He repeated to him what he had said, and he nudged him with his foot and said: ʿO Allah, grant him well beingʿ or “O Allah, heal him.” - Shuʿbah was not certain. He [‘Ali] said: And I never suffered that sickness again after that. (Using translation from Aḥmad 841)"
"6941","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When this verse was revealed: \""O you who believe! When you consult the Messenger in private, offer something in charity before your private consultation.\"" What was meant was to offer charity. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me: What do you think, should this charity be one dinar? I said: People will not be able to afford that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Then how much sho"
"6942","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When this verse was revealed: \""O you who believe! When you consult the Messenger in private, offer something in charity before your consultation.\"" The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): O Ali, tell the people to give charity (i.e., to offer something in charity). He asked: O Messenger of Allah! How much? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:"
"6943","The narrator says) If you count the Caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) as two years, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) as ten years, Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) as twelve years, and Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) as six years, (this makes a total of 30 years). Ali bin Ziyad says: I asked Hammad bin Salamah: Are these words ""if you count"" from Sayyiduna Safinah (may Allah be pleased with him)? He replied: Yes."
"6944","I am ruined, I have been destroyed. He asked: How is that? He said: I proposed marriage to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from me. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Stay where you are, I will go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and make the same request as you did. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sat before him, and said: O Messenger of Allah! You are aware of my goodwill and my early acceptance of Islam, and I have such and such qualities. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Then what happened? He said: Marry me to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) returned to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is waiting for Allah’s command regarding Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her). Come with us to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), so that he may make the same request as we did. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Both of them came to me while I was working among my small date palm trees. They said: We have come to you with a marriage proposal from your cousin (i.e., the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: They made me aware of the situation, so I stood up, dragging my cloak, until I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat before him. I said: O Messenger of Allah! You are aware of my early acceptance of Islam and my goodwill, and I have such and such qualities. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Then what happened? I said: Marry me to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Do you have anything (to give as mahr)? I said: I have my horse and my camel. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for your horse, it is necessary for you to keep it, but as for your camel, you may sell it. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: So I sold it for 480 (dirhams or dinars), brought it, and placed it in the lap of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it in his hand and said: O Bilal, buy perfume for us with this. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed that the dowry for Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) be prepared. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a bed made for her and a pillow made of leather stuffed with palm fibers. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): When she comes to you, do not speak to her before I come. Then Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) came (to Sayyiduna Ali’s house) with Sayyidah Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her), until she sat in one corner of the house and I sat in another corner. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived and asked: Where is my brother? Sayyidah Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her) said: He is your brother, and you have married your daughter to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house and said to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her): Bring me water. So she went to the water vessel in the house and brought water. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it, rinsed his mouth with it once, then said to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her): Come forward! She came forward, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sprinkled that water on her chest and head and said (i.e., made this supplication): “O Allah! I seek Your protection for her and her offspring from the accursed devil.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her): Turn to the other side. She turned to the other side, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sprinkled water between her shoulders and said (i.e., supplicated): “O Allah! I seek Your protection for her and her offspring from the accursed devil.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me water. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I did as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished; I got up, filled the vessel with water, and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rinsed his mouth with it, then said to me: Come forward. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sprinkled water on my head and chest and supplicated: “O Allah! I seek Your protection for him and his offspring from the accursed devil.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Turn to the other side. I turned to the other side, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sprinkled water between my shoulders and supplicated: “O Allah! I seek Your protection for him and his offspring from the accursed devil.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): “Live with your wife in the name of Allah, seeking blessing and with blessing.”"
"6945","When Ali married Fatimah, the Prophet ﷺ said to him: Give her something. He said: I have nothing with me. He said: Where is your Hutamiyyah (coat of mail). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2125)"
"6946","narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) gave an iron armor as mahr to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"6947","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Fatimah a trousseau of a velvet garment, a waterskin and a leather pillow stuffed with idhkhir fibres. (Using translation from Aḥmad 643)"
"6948","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a marriage proposal for Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), but the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""She is young."" Then Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a proposal for her, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) married her to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6949","narrates: When the son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Sayyiduna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him), passed away, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There is a wet nurse for him in Paradise.”"
"6950","I have never seen anyone more kind to one's family than Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Ibrahim was sent to the suburb of Medina for suckling. He used to go there and we accompanied him. He entered the house, and it was filled with smoke as his foster-father was a bricksmith. He took him (his son Ibrihim) and kissed him and then came back. 'Amr said that when Ibrihim died. Allah's LMessenger ﷺ said: Ibrihim is my son and he dies as a suckling babe. He has now two foster-mothers who would complete his suckling period in Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 2316)"
"6951","that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Sufficient for you among the women of mankind are Mariam bint 'Imran, Khadijah bint Khuwailid, Fatimah bint Muhammad and Asiyah the wife of Fir'awn."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3878)"
"6952","I said to Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah: I saw you lean towards the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) during his illness, and then you began to weep. Then you leaned towards the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) a second time and began to laugh. Lady Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) explained: When I leaned towards him, he (peace and blessings be upon him) told me that he was about to pass away, so I began to weep. Then when I leaned towards him a second time, he (peace and blessings be upon him) told me that among his household, I would be the first to join him, and that I am the leader of all the women of Paradise, except that the case of Lady Maryam bint Imran is different. At this, I laughed."
"6953","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) whispered something to her, and she began to weep. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) whispered something else to her, and she began to laugh. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I used to think that this woman had superiority over others (meaning she was more intelligent than others), but she turned out to be just a woman—she was crying one moment and laughing the next. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, I asked her about this. She replied: First, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) whispered to me that he was about to pass away, so I wept. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) whispered to me that among his family, I would be the first to join him, so I laughed."
"6954","I asked Fatimah about this, and she replied: The Prophet (peace be upon him) first whispered to me that he would pass away during this illness, so I began to weep. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) whispered to me that I would be the first among his family to join him, so I laughed."
"6955","Al Miswar bin Makramah said that he heard the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ say on the pulpit Banu Hashim bin Al Mughirah sought permission from me to marry their daughter to ‘Ali bin Abi Talib. But I do not permit, again, I do not permit, again, I do not permit except that Ibn Abi Talib divorces my daughter and marries their daughter. My daughter is my part, what makes her uneasy makes me uneasy and what troubles her troubles me. The full information rests with the tradition narrated by Ahmad. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2071)"
"6956","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying this: At that time, I was near the age of puberty. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Fatimah is a part of me, and I fear that she will be put to trial regarding her religion. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned his son-in-law from the Banu Abd Shams and praised his conduct as a son-in-law and spoke well of him. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whenever he spoke to me, he spoke the truth, and whenever he made a promise to me, he fulfilled it. I do not declare anything lawful as unlawful, nor do I declare anything unlawful as lawful, but the daughter of Allah’s Messenger and the daughter of Allah’s enemy can never be together in one place."
"6957","The daughter of the Messenger of Allah and the daughter of the enemy of Allah cannot be together with any Muslim man."" So Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) refrained from that marriage proposal."
"6958","When al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb [which means war], then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: ʿShow me my son; what did you name him?ʿ We said: Harb. He said: ʿRather he is Hasan.” When al-Husain was born, I named him Harb, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: “Show me my son; what did you name him?” We said; Harb. He said: “Rather he is Husain.” When the third one was born, I named him Harb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said: “Show me my son, what did you name him?” I said. Harb. He said: ʿRather, he is Muhassin.ʿ Then he said: ʿI have named them after the fashion of the sons of Haroon, Shabbar and Shabeer and Mushabbir.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 769)"
"6959","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise, except for two maternal cousins, 'Isa ibn Maryam and Yahya ibn Zakariya (whose case is different)."
"6960","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: An angel came before me who had sought permission from his Lord to send salutations upon me. That angel gave me the glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise."
"6961","I show mercy to both of them, so You also show mercy to both of them."
"6962","I saw Hasan b. 'Ali upon the shoulders of Allah's Apostle ﷺ and he was saying: O Allah, I love him, and love him Thou. (Using translation from Muslim 2422a)"
"6963","The Prophet (peace be upon him) turned to one side, and I also turned with him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Call Hasan to me. So Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) came walking, and there was a necklace around his neck. The Prophet (peace be upon him) gestured with his blessed hand in this way, and Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) also gestured with his hand in the same way. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) took hold of him and said: O Allah! I love him, so You also love him, and love the one who loves him. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: To me, after the statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him) which he made, there is no one more beloved than Sayyiduna Imam Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Abdullah bin Muhammad narrated these words to us with the letters “sh” and “h”, although the original word is “sakhab”, that is, with “d” and “kh”."
"6964","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in prayer. Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) came—he was a small child at that time. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went into prostration, he climbed onto the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) neck and back. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gently raised his head until he had seated him on the ground. The people said: O Messenger of Allah! We have seen you do something with this child that we have not seen you do with anyone else. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He is my fragrance in this world; this son of mine is a leader. Soon Allah, the Exalted, will bring reconciliation between two great groups of Muslims because of him."
"6965","The narrator says: So he lifted the cloth from his stomach and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) kissed his navel. (The narrator says:) If the navel had been included in the area of covering ('awrah), then Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) would not have lifted the cloth from it."
"6966","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The (funeral) prayer should be offered for a child.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1507)"
"6967","""I came to the Prophet ﷺ one night concerning some need, so the Prophet ﷺ came out while he was covering up something, and I did not know what it was. Once I had tended to my need, I said: 'What is this that you were covering up?' So he uncovered it, and I found it was Hasan and Husain [peace be upon them] upon his hips. So he said: 'These are my two sons, and the sons of my daughter. O Allah! Indeed, I love them, so love them, and love those who love them.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3769)"
"6968","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) received the news—while he was present at his lands—that Sayyiduna Imam Husa"
"6969","A person asked ʿAbdullah bin ʿUmar whether a Muslim could kill flies. I heard him saying (in reply). ""The people of Iraq are asking about the killing of flies while they themselves murdered the son of the daughter of Messenger of Allah ﷺ . The Prophet ﷺ said, They (i.e. Hasan and Husain) are my two sweet basils in this world."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3753)"
"6970","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was performing prayer when Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) climbed onto his back. The people tried to move them away, but the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Let them be, may my parents be sacrificed for them. Whoever loves me should also love these two."
"6971","Sayyiduna Husayn (may All"
"6972","I was present with Ibn Ziyad when the head of Sayyiduna Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought. He touched his nose with his stick and said: I have never seen a person as beautiful as this. So I said: He most closely resembled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6973","None resembled the Prophet ﷺ more than Al-Hasan bin ʿAli did. (Using translation from Bukhārī 3752)"
"6974","Al-Hasan ؓ most closely resembles the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the chest and head, and Al-Husain ؓ most closely resembles the Prophet ﷺ in what is lower than that. (Using translation from Aḥmad 774)"
"6975","I not see you doing this with the child? By Allah, I also have children whose faces have appeared, but I have never kissed any of them.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"
"6976","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat on the bedding. He seated Lady Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) on his right, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) on his left, and Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) in front of him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited (this verse): “O People of the House! Allah only wishes to remove impurity from you and to purify you thoroughly.” Then he said: “O Allah! These are my Ahl al-Bayt (family).” Sayyiduna Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He said from the edge of the house, “O Messenger of Allah! Am I also among your Ahl al-Bayt?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “You are also among my Ahl al-Bayt.” Sayyiduna Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Of all the things I could have hoped for, this was the most remarkable."
"6977","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali, Fatimah, Al-Hasan and Al-Husain: ""I am at war with whoever makes war with you, and peace for whoever makes peace with you."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3870)"
"6978","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul! Whoever harbors enmity against us, the Ahl al-Bayt, Allah Almighty will admit him into Hell."
"6979","I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Talhah has made Paradise obligatory for himself.” Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) to come to the cistern. He brought water to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his shield. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to drink from it, but he sensed an odor in it, so he did not drink it. Then, with that water, the blood on the face of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was washed away. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The wrath of Allah will descend most severely upon those who have bloodied the face of Allah’s Messenger.”"
"6980","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take care of your brother, who has made Paradise obligatory for himself."" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: An arrow had struck the face and cheek of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). I intended to remove the arrow from the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), but Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: ""I beseech you by Allah, leave this task for me."" So I left it for him. Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) caught the arrow with his mouth and tried to pull it out; he disliked that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) should suffer any pain. Then he pulled it out with his mouth. Then I moved towards the other arrow, which was stuck in the cheek of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), to remove it. Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Abu Bakr, I beseech you by Allah, leave this for me."" So he also caught that arrow with his mouth and tried to pull it out; he disliked causing any pain to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Then he pulled it out. Sayyiduna Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) was more wounded than the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) (or he participated more in the fight), while the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was more severely affected. Sayyiduna Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) received more than thirty wounds from spears, swords, and arrows that day."
"6981","Sayyiduna Talha bin Ubaidullah (may Allah be pleased with him), which had become paralyzed; he was protecting the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) with it on the day of the Battle of Uhud."
"6982","I may narrate it from you, because all the children of the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate hadith from their fathers. So he said: O my son, whoever has spent time in the company of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I too have spent the same or even more time with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). O my son, you know that your mother Asma bint Abu Bakr was my wife, and you also know that Aisha bint Abu Bakr is your maternal aunt, and you also know that my mother is Safiyyah bint Abdul Muttalib (who is the paternal aunt of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my uncles are Hamzah bin Abdul Muttalib and Abu Talib, and Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is also my cousin. You also know that Khadijah bint Khuwaylid was my paternal aunt; she was the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the daughter of Sayyidah Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) is Sayyiduna Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), who is the daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And you also know that the mother of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is Sayyidah Aminah bint Wahb (may Allah be pleased with her), while (my mother) Sayyidah Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) and (my uncle) Sayyiduna Hamzah (may Allah be pleased with him), their mother is Halah bint Wahb (who is the real maternal aunt of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So, all praise is due to Allah, I have remained with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a good manner. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever attributes to me something which I have not said, let him prepare his abode in the Hellfire."
"6983","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) climbed the (mountain of) Hira. Along with him were Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, Sayyiduna Umar, Sayyiduna Uthman, Sayyiduna Ali, Sayyiduna Talhah, and Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them). In the presence of these individuals, the mountain began to shake, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Hira, remain still, for upon you is a Prophet, a Siddiq, and a martyr.”"
"6984","from Az-Zubair, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered together his parents for me the Day of Quraizah, (i.e. the battle of Ahzab) and said: 'May my mother and father be ransomed for you.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3743)"
"6985","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: On the day of the Battle of the Trench, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Who will bring me information about Banu Qurayza? Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I will. Then he mounted his horse and brought information about them. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said this a second time, so Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I will. The P"
"6986","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I wish that some righteous person from among my companions would guard me tonight."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: While we were in this state, I heard the sound of a weapon. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Who is it?"" He replied: ""Sa'd bin Malik."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Why have you come?"" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have come to guard you."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) snoring during his sleep (that is, then he slept peacefully)."
"6987","Saʿd reported that on the Day of Uhud I saw on the right side of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and on his left side two persons dressed in white clothes and whom I did not see before nor after that, and they were Gabriel and Michael (Allah be pleased with both of them). (Using translation from Muslim 2306a)"
"6988","I have never heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) combine his parents for anyone except Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him), because on the day of the Battle of Uhud, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: Shoot (arrows), may my parents be sacrificed for you."
"6989","By Allah, I am the first person amongst the Arabs to throw an arrow in the cause of Allah and we used to go with Messenger of Allah ﷺ and there was no food for us to eat but only the leaves of hubla and samur trees (they are wild trees) and as a result thereof one amongst us would relieve himself as does the goat. (How strange it is) that now the people of Banu Asad (the progeny of Zubair) instruct me in religion and try to impose punishment upon me (in regard to it). If it is so (that I am so ignorant of religion), then indeed, I am undone and my deeds have been lost. Ibn Numair, however, did not make a mention of the word (idhan) thus? (in his narration). (Using translation from Muslim 2966a)"
"6990","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made a supplication, “O Allah! Whenever he supplicates to You, answer him.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was referring to Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6991","The narrator says: Each one of us wished that the person entering would be from his own family, then Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived."
